From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:31:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] input: apply Gnoblin device preferences from live config

Apply the Gnoblin device preferences to the input settings from the live config.

The settings that older GNOME schemas lack (custom acceleration and the other optional keys) are read only when the
schema has them, and the custom pointer profile survives older schemas. A missing optional setting falls back to
the default acceleration without a warning. Only an explicit numlock-state override keeps Num Lock state in
memory; otherwise GNOME persistence stays active.
